  "notes": [
    "Row bounds are the damage authority; dirtyRows summarizes how many are nonempty. No former broad interval remains in source or observers.",
    "Core tests cover 1x1, 3-column, 40x24 and 80x30; the 80x30 cell buffer crosses a CPU bank and a host snapshot oracle verifies scroll bytes and guards.",
    "Sparse edits on rows 0 and 29 preserve intervening rows; stale generation acknowledgements retain newer damage and oldestDamage persists until all damage is presented.",
    "Text admission remains 40x24. ScreenWidth/ScreenHeight return zero outside ready/accepting state.",
    "Cooked input retains the existing maximum 36-character tail. At most 110 echo bytes are generated, so its 128-byte buffer remains sufficient; the adapter narrows to available columns, tested at width three. No cooked-session allocation increases.",
    "Raw/optimized presentation, focus, capture, cancellation, lifecycle, allocation-failure and caller-retention checks pass.",
    "Optimized isolated text-console visible scroll is 13.75 ms average in this run versus B0 11.25 ms; this is not bitmap scroll or a hosted qualification claim."
